\details{
Idempotent and safe to call unconditionally at the same points
\code{.ensure_audit_tables()}/schema-initialization already run: it
first checks whether the stored constraint already covers every
current \code{.audit_event_types} value and returns immediately if so,
so a database created (or already migrated) under the current
event type list pays only the cost of that one check.

SQLite and DuckDB have no \verb{ALTER TABLE ... DROP/ADD CONSTRAINT}
(confirmed directly: DuckDB raises "Not implemented ... No support
for that ALTER TABLE option yet!"), so both rebuild the table
rather than alter it in place, via SQLite's own documented
procedure for schema changes a plain \verb{ALTER TABLE} cannot express:
create the replacement under a temporary name, copy every row
across by explicit column list (preserving \code{audit_id} values
exactly, since \code{audit_events.audit_id} and \code{audit_chain.audit_id}
both hold foreign keys to them), drop the original, then rename
the replacement into place.

On SQLite, only \code{audit_log} itself needs rebuilding: at no point
does the name \code{audit_log} stop existing except between the \code{DROP}
and the final \code{RENAME}, both inside the same transaction, and the
original is never renamed away first (which would risk SQLite
silently rewriting \code{audit_events}'/\code{audit_chain}'s \verb{REFERENCES audit_log(...)} clauses to point at the archived table instead).
\verb{PRAGMA foreign_keys} must also be turned off around the whole
operation (and, being a documented no-op inside a transaction, set
before \code{.with_db_transaction()} opens one): with it on (the
default this package connects with), \verb{DROP TABLE audit_log} itself
fails outright -- confirmed directly -- because \code{audit_events}/
\code{audit_chain} still reference it. SQLite's append-only triggers
(\code{.audit_trigger_names}) are owned by the table they are defined
on and so do not survive a \verb{DROP TABLE}; \code{.protect_audit_tables()}
re-creates them (via \verb{CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS}) once the
rebuild is complete.

DuckDB has no \verb{PRAGMA foreign_keys} equivalent at all (confirmed:
no such setting appears in \code{duckdb_settings()}) and refuses to
drop \code{audit_log} outright while \code{audit_events}/\code{audit_chain} still
reference it ("Catalog Error: Could not drop the table because
this table is main key table of the table 'audit_events'",
confirmed directly); it also refuses to rename a from-scratch
replacement table into place while anything still references it
